# Kira Nerys, Firebrand: "If a creature you control would enter while you control an attacking creature, instead it
# enters tapped and attacking" (CR 614.1d, 508.4). The token is put into the combat as it arrives, attacking what its
# controller chooses (here the only thing it could attack), so the combat holds two attackers.
# Kira is cast on turn 1 with a Mox Ruby, a Mox Pearl and a Mox Jet ({1}{R}{W}) beside an Ornithopter, which attacks on turn
# 3. In the declare attackers step, while it is attacking, Secure the Wastes makes one Warrior token: it is a creature Bot1
# controls, so Kira's replacement makes it enter tapped and attacking (never declared, so nothing that watches attackers
# being declared sees it).

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Ruby
Mox Pearl
Mox Jet
Kira Nerys, Firebrand
Ornithopter
Secure the Wastes
Island
Island x13

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Kira Nerys, Firebrand.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Attack(Ornithopter > Bot2)
? Combat.Attackers.Count = 1
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Secure the Wastes.Cast(X: 1)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot1.Battlefield.Warrior Token.Tapped = true
? Combat.Attackers.Count = 2

[Expect]
Combat.Attackers.Count = 2
Bot1.Battlefield.Warrior Token.Tapped = true
Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Tapped = true
